For this card's third part, as the ruling's execution section says:
- one objectui PR (`Part of objectui#7611`): a field widget that lists one registry type by name and stores the name only, the objectui#12136 / objectstack#22794 mechanism reachable from record forms;
- one objectstack PR: move `.objectui-sha` to the head carrying the widget, declare it on the name field of the position grant and of the permission-set grant, delete the two `add` blocks on `sys-user.page.ts` (objectstack#22863 has merged, so nothing is waited on);
- Q3b: one objectui PR on the read side, listing positions for a `{ source: 'registry', type }` approver binding from the registry and storing the name only; no authoring surface touched; the loosened type goes when objectui moves to spec 18;
- the dev measures first, in the browser, whether the two grant tables' related lists on the user page offer "new" and whether the row-level "remove" survives without `add`; if "remove" disappears, report first, add nothing.
- Both land before 6b-2. A, A' and B1 were not taken; the decision card is closed `completed`.
